<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img class="bg" src="/assets/img/photos/conference-room.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/conference-room-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/conference-room.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.1"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Appraisal questions</span></nav><p class="kicker">Answers by topic</p><h1>Insurance Appraisal Questions from Illinois Owners</h1><p class="lede">Plain answers to the questions we hear most — about the process, costs, timing and the Illinois rules around it.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn line-light" href="/contact-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose"><nav class="jump" aria-label="FAQ topics"><ul><li><a href="#faq-0">Appraisal basics</a></li><li><a href="#faq-1">Costs and fees</a></li><li><a href="#faq-2">Timing and deadlines</a></li><li><a href="#faq-3">Illinois specifics</a></li><li><a href="#faq-4">Working with us</a></li></ul></nav><h2 id="faq-0">Appraisal basics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What is insurance appraisal?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>A process written into most property policies for resolving disagreements about the amount of a covered loss. Each side names an appraiser, the appraisers pick an umpire, and an agreement signed by any two of the three sets the amount.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is appraisal the same as arbitration?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>They’re similar but not identical. Appraisal is limited to the amount of loss and is usually less formal, with no discovery or testimony under oath. Courts treat the two differently in some respects.</p></div></details><details><summary>Who can demand appraisal?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Under most policies, either you or the insurer can demand appraisal in writing once you disagree on the amount of loss.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does every Illinois policy have an appraisal clause?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Most homeowners, condo, landlord and commercial property policies do. Some forms modify or omit it, so read your own policy’s conditions section.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-1">Costs and fees</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How much does an appraiser cost?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Fee arrangements vary: flat fees, hourly rates, or a percentage of the increase. Each side pays its own appraiser. Get the arrangement in writing before work starts.</p></div></details><details><summary>Who pays the umpire?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Usually the policyholder and the insurer split the umpire’s fee evenly.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is appraisal worth it for a small gap?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Often not. If the gap is only a few thousand dollars, a documented supplement request may close it more cheaply. Our disputed-amount estimator helps you weigh the numbers.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-2">Timing and deadlines</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How long does appraisal take?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Many residential appraisals finish in six to sixteen weeks after both appraisers are named. Large commercial losses or umpire hearings can take longer.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does appraisal stop my lawsuit deadline?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Not automatically. Illinois law can pause the limitation period between the time you file a proof of loss and the insurer’s denial, but how that applies depends on your facts. Talk to an attorney well before any deadline.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is there a deadline to demand appraisal?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Some policies set one; many don’t. Courts may also consider whether a demand was made within a reasonable time. Don’t wait longer than you need to.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-3">Illinois specifics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who regulates insurers in Illinois?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>The Illinois Department of Insurance. It licenses insurers and adjusters and accepts consumer complaints about claim handling.</p></div></details><details><summary>What is Section 155?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Section 155 of the Illinois Insurance Code allows a court, in a lawsuit, to award attorney fees and a limited additional amount when an insurer’s delay or refusal to pay is found to be vexatious and unreasonable. It’s a legal remedy decided by courts, not by an appraisal panel. Talk to an attorney about whether it applies to you.</p></div></details><details><summary>What is the Illinois FAIR Plan?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>The Illinois FAIR Plan Association provides basic property insurance for owners who can’t get coverage in the regular market. FAIR Plan policies have their own forms and conditions, which may handle disputes differently.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does Illinois have a wind pool?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>No. Illinois doesn’t have a separate state wind pool. Wind and hail are typically covered under standard homeowners and commercial policies, sometimes with separate deductibles.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-4">Working with us</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Are you public adjusters or attorneys?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Neither. We provide appraisal, estimate review and umpire services. We don’t negotiate claims outside appraisal or give legal advice.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can you work with my contractor or attorney?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Yes. We often work alongside contractors, public adjusters and attorneys, while serving in one defined role on each claim.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you serve all of Illinois?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Yes. We work in all 102 Illinois counties, with regular work in the Chicago area, the Fox Valley, Rockford, Peoria, Springfield, Champaign–Urbana, Bloomington–Normal and the Metro East.</p></div></details></div></article>
<aside class="aside"><div class="box box-call"><h2 class="box-t">Talk it through first</h2><p>The first conversation is free. We’ll tell you plainly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="big" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn full" href="/contact-an-appraiser/">Send claim details</a></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-t">Resources</h2><ul class="box-list"><li><a href="/illinois-appraisal-process/">Illinois appraisal process</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-questions/" aria-current="page">Appraisal questions</a></li><li><a href="/insurance-claim-terms/">Claim terms glossary</a></li><li><a href="/policyholder-articles/">Policyholder articles</a></li></ul></div></aside></div><section class="band"><div class="wrap band-in rv"><div><h2>Didn’t see your question?</h2><p>Call or email — we’re glad to talk it through.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn dark" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn line-dark" href="/contact-an-appraiser/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
